contentText:
There appears to be some bad blood among the past and current members of family country group The Band Perry .

The trio launched in 2010 as a sibling trio, consisting of Kimberly, Reid and Neil Perry, and earned hits including &#8220;If I Die Young&#8221; (a Hot Country Songs and Adult Contemporary No. 1) and &#8220;Better Dig Two&#8221; (No. 1 on Hot Country Songs and Country Airplay). The group went on hiatus in 2023, and Kimberly launched a brief solo career, before The Band Perry regrouped with Kimberly, brother Reid and Kimberly&#8217;s husband, Johnny Costello. Soon, Reid left the band and it transitioned to a duo with Kimberly and her husband, who released singles including &#8220;Psychological.&#8221;

